From 9d2559a0ea24aa7879c39a8f77fc71a909b3aeb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 09:20:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 129/131] netstack: addr/rm and an event on ifaces/<name>/link
 (#764)

netcfg gets ifaces/<name>/addr/rm: any write removes the interface's
address and every route through it, also a default route. netstack reads
each device's link (the driver keeps it) at most every 500 ms from its
poll and, when it changed, posts an event to readers of
ifaces/<name>/link, so dhcpd can wait for a link instead of asking again.
Step 1 of RFC 0004 in redox-rpi.
